  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Faisal Ainul Haque Siddiqui vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Author: N. R. Borkar Bench: Prakash D. Naik, N. R. Borkar 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 3989 Of 2024 Harishankar Rampravesh Singh ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Respondent With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 982 Of 2024 Chhotu Ramkumar Singh ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Respondent With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 983 Of 2024 Vikas Umakant Chaudhary ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra And Anr.. ...Respondents With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 992 Of 2024 Chandan Umakant Chaudhary ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Respondent With Versus State Of Maharashtra ... Respondent With Faisal Ainul Haque Siddiqui vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/96014184/ 1 Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 1472 Of 2024 Mohammad Ibrahim Shaikh ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Respondent Sunny Thote 1 of 3 ::: Uploaded on - 15/04/2024 ::: Downloaded on - 27/04/2024 01:52:39 ::: 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc With Psi, Takmoye, Pant Nagar Police Station. Mr. Swapnil B., Kashimire Police Station. Api, R.C. Powar, Manor Police Station, Palghar in Wp/2747/2024. Mr. Sajay Reday, Psi, Crime Branch, Navi Mumbai Police Station in Wp/326/2024 .... Coram : Prakash D. Naik, & N. R. Borkar, Jj. Date : 10th April, 2024. P.C.: 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "In all these matters the Petitioners have raised the issue of applicability of Section 328 of Indian Faisal Ainul Haque Siddiqui vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/96014184/ 2 Penal Code and non maintainability of simultaneous proceedings for the offences under SUNNY THOTE 2 of 3 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc the Indian Penal Code and Food Safety and Standards Act. 2. Learned Counsel for the Petitioners has relied upon the decision of Apex Court in the case of Ram Nath V/s. State of Uttar Pradesh and Others, 2024 SCC OnLine SC 177. 3. Mr. Sonawane also submitted that the issue about applicability of Section 328 of Indian Penal Code in such cases is pending before the Apex Court and decision is likely to be delivered shortly and hence the matters be adjourned beyond vacation.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "In all these matters the Petitioners have raised the issue of applicability of Section 328 of Indian Faisal Ainul Haque Siddiqui vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/96014184/ 2 Penal Code and non maintainability of simultaneous proceedings for the offences under SUNNY THOTE 2 of 3 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc the Indian Penal Code and Food Safety and Standards Act. 2. Learned Counsel for the Petitioners has relied upon the decision of Apex Court in the case of Ram Nath V/s. State of Uttar Pradesh and Others, 2024 SCC OnLine SC 177. 3. Mr. Sonawane also submitted that the issue about applicability of Section 328 of Indian Penal Code in such cases is pending before the Apex Court and decision is likely to be delivered shortly and hence the matters be adjourned beyond vacation.",
